    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Core Rulebook</i></p><p><i>See also: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Feats\" title=\"Feats\">Feats</a></i></p><p>You are particularly skilled at <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Aiming\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Aiming\">Aiming</a> your attacks.</p><p><b>Prerequisites:</b> <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Point-Blank_Shot\" title=\"Point-Blank Shot\">Point-Blank Shot</a> Feat, <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Base_Attack_Bonus\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Base Attack Bonus\">Base Attack Bonus</a> +2</p><p><b>Effect:</b> If you <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Aim\" title=\"Aim\">Aim</a> before making a ranged attack, you gain a +1 bonus on your attack roll.</p><p><b>Special:</b> A <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pilot_(Vehicle_Combat)\" title=\"Pilot (Vehicle Combat)\">Pilot</a> can use this Feat, but since they must spend at least one <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Move_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Move Action\">Move Action</a> operating their <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vehicles\" title=\"Vehicles\">Vehicles</a>, they must split their <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Aim\" title=\"Aim\">Aim</a> (two <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Swift_Actions\" title=\"Swift Actions\">Swift Actions</a>) and attack (<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Standard_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Standard Action\">Standard Action</a>) into two separate turns, making it more likely that the target will break line of sight or avoid you.</p>",
